## 10. Final go/no-go test

Before submitting, verify these six things in a single test session.

- A user funds the demo wallet through PayPal Sandbox.
- The backend issues an offline spending authorization within the reserved limit.
- A merchant accepts a payment in the offline flow.
- After reconnection, the system synchronizes the payment and runs fraud assessment.
- The legitimate payment settles correctly, while a suspicious test case receives the documented risk action.
- The public repository, setup instructions and demo video accurately reflect the working implementation.

If one of the first five fails, fix that before spending time on visual polish.

The most important principle: your hackathon project is not finished merely because all the services exist. It is finished when the complete flow works, the AI's contribution is measured, the failure cases are understood, and a judge can reproduce the result.